DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzppooooll__iinnfflluuxxddbb produces InfluxDB-line-protocol-compatible metrics from
     zpools.  Like the zzppooooll command, zzppooooll__iinnfflluuxxddbb reads the current pool
     status and statistics.  Unlike the zzppooooll command which is intended for
     humans, zzppooooll__iinnfflluuxxddbb formats the output in the InfluxDB line protocol.
     The expected use is as a plugin to a metrics collector or aggregator,
     such as Telegraf.

     By default, zzppooooll__iinnfflluuxxddbb prints pool metrics and status in the InfluxDB
     line protocol format.  All pools are printed, similar to the zzppooooll ssttaattuuss
     command.  Providing a pool name restricts the output to the named pool.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     --ee, ----eexxeeccdd  Run in daemon mode compatible with Telegraf's eexxeeccdd plugin.
                  In this mode, the pools are sampled every time a newline ap‐
                  pears on the standard input.

     --nn, ----nnoo--hhiissttooggrraamm
                  Do not print latency and I/O size histograms.  This can re‐
                  duce the total amount of data, but one should consider the
                  value brought by the insights that latency and I/O size dis‐
                  tributions provide.  The resulting values are suitable for
                  graphing with Grafana's heatmap plugin.

     --ss, ----ssuumm--hhiissttooggrraamm--bbuucckkeettss
                  Accumulates bucket values.  By default, the values are not
                  accumulated and the raw data appears as shown by zzppooooll
                  iioossttaatt.  This works well for Grafana's heatmap plugin.  Sum‐
                  ming the buckets produces output similar to Prometheus his‐
                  tograms.

     --tt, ----ttaaggss _k_e_y=_v_a_l_u_e[,_k_e_y=_v_a_l_u_e]â¦
                  Adds specified tags to the tag set.  No sanity checking is
                  performed.  See the InfluxDB Line Protocol format documenta‐
                  tion for details on escaping special characters used in
                  tags.

     --hh, ----hheellpp   Print a usage summary.

